Supported formats include (non-exhaustive):
  ISO-style:       2024-03-15, 2024/03/15, 2024.03.15
  US-style:        03/15/2024, 3-15-2024
  Long month name: March 15, 2024 / 15 March 2024
  Short month name: Mar 15, 2024 / 15 Mar 2024
  Two-digit year:  03/15/24  → interpreted with datetime.strptime century logic
  ...and more via dateutil / brute-force strptime scanning.

Stdlib only (no dateutil).  We use a large list of strptime format strings plus
a custom long-form parser.
